From: NeoDarwin
Subject: [PATCH] iokit: publish hidden media only when the IOMedia class exists

IOService::publishHiddenMedia() looks up the IOMedia metaclass and only
asserts that it exists: on Apple systems IOStorageFamily is always in the
kernelcache. NeoDarwin's SBSA kernel roots on a memory device (md0, a BSD
device from bsd/dev/memdev.c) before any storage family is loaded, so the
lookup returns NULL, and the RELEASE kernel, with the assert compiled out,
faulted in OSMetaClass::applyToInstances() as soon as IOFindBSDRoot had
chosen md0 (found at the first mockfs boot, P1-07). Without the class there
are no IOMedia objects to publish; the function now skips the walk.

Rebase-risk: low (one condition).
---
diff --git a/iokit/Kernel/IOService.cpp b/iokit/Kernel/IOService.cpp
--- a/iokit/Kernel/IOService.cpp
+++ b/iokit/Kernel/IOService.cpp
@@ -5368,8 +5368,8 @@
 	const OSMetaClass * iomediaClass;
 	bool                wasHiding;
 
+	/* NULL until IOStorageFamily is loaded; then there is no IOMedia to publish. */
 	iomediaClass = OSMetaClass::getMetaClassWithName(gIOMediaKey);
-	assert(iomediaClass);
 
 	LOCKWRITENOTIFY();
 	wasHiding = gIOServiceHideIOMedia;
@@ -5380,7 +5380,7 @@
 
 	FindRootMediaContext ctx = { .services = NULL, .parent = parent };
 
-	if (wasHiding) {
+	if (wasHiding && iomediaClass) {
 		iomediaClass->applyToInstances(publishHiddenMediaApplier, &ctx);
 	}
 	if (ctx.services) {
